body:
Hello,
When building the DSN here : http://api.cakephp.org/3.0/source-class-Cake.Database.Driver.Postgres.html#61

I believe that as soon as you define 'host=' in the DSN it will attempt to connect over TCP and not directly to the unix socket.  

Some examples:
All of these tests have been performed after disabling TCP communication on localhost over default port on linux server and postgres where linux user and postgres user exists.  

Connects properly over socket

``` php
// config/app.php
'Datasources' => [
        'default' => [
            'className' => 'Cake\Database\Connection',
            'driver' => 'Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres',
            'database' => 'cake',
            'username' => 'user',
     ]
],
// \Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres
$dsn = "pgsql:dbname={$config['database']}";
```

Correctly fails when not defining the user with error: Error: SQLSTATE[08006] [7] FATAL: Peer authentication failed for user "root" 

``` php
// config/app.php
'Datasources' => [
        'default' => [
            'className' => 'Cake\Database\Connection',
            'driver' => 'Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres',
            'database' => 'cake',
            // 'username' => 'user',
     ]
],

// \Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres
$dsn = "pgsql:dbname={$config['database']}";
```

Connection times out : Error: SQLSTATE[08006] [7] timeout expired 
This is expected as the DSN as defined is attempting to connect to localhost over TCP which has been disabled on test server via linux firewall 

``` php
// config/app.php
'Datasources' => [
        'default' => [
            'className' => 'Cake\Database\Connection',
            'driver' => 'Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres',
            'database' => 'cake',
            'username' => 'user',

            'host' => 'localhost',
     ]
],

// \Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres
$dsn = "pgsql:host={$config['host']};port={$config['port']};dbname={$config['database']}";
```

Fails with error:  Error: SQLSTATE[08006] [7] could not translate host name "port=5432" to address: Name or service not known 

``` php
// config/app.php
'Datasources' => [
        'default' => [
            'className' => 'Cake\Database\Connection',
            'driver' => 'Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres',
            'database' => 'cake',
            'username' => 'user',

            'host' => '',
            'unix_socket' => true, // as suggested above by oldskool, with or without this setting the same error occurs
     ]
],

// \Cake\Database\Driver\Postgres
$dsn = "pgsql:host={$config['host']};port={$config['port']};dbname={$config['database']}";
```

Per the docs:  http://book.cakephp.org/3.0/en/orm/database-basics.html#configuration

If I "leave the host key blank"  the default $_baseConfig will write 'host' => 'localhost' by default
http://api.cakephp.org/3.0/source-class-Cake.Database.Driver.Postgres.html#31
